<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I imagining how they feel, or how I would feel in their place?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Which of my beliefs about their view have I actually checked with them?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I asked a question I don't already know the answer to?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is there an option that meets what they want as well as what I want?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "I sketch what their fortnight probably looked like, note that I'm guessing, then ask privately how the project is going from their side. It turns out a second project landed on them without my knowing; we reprioritise together." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "I decide they've stopped caring, picture how I'd feel if I were slacking, and send a sharp message about accountability." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A team lead notices that a usually reliable colleague has missed two deadlines in a row and seems curt in meetings." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Imagining their side softened my reaction, but only asking told me what was actually going on; taking and getting perspective together led to a fair and workable fix." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Before you respond, name your own first reading of the situation so you can set it aside for a moment." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Imagine the other person's day, constraints and goals, and ask what they know that you don't and what they want from this." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Write down two or three guesses about how they see it, and mark each one as a guess." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Check the guesses by asking open questions (\"How does this look from where you sit?\") and listen without rebutting." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Revise your reading with what you heard, then decide what to do, looking for an option that serves both of you." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Perspective-taking" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Practice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Perspective-taking" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "imagine-other perspective taking" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "putting yourself in someone else's shoes" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "taking another's perspective" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/social-cognition> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Deliberately imagining a situation from another person's point of view, including what they know, want and feel, as a way to understand them and connect with them; best paired with simply asking them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/compassion-and-relationships> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Perspective-taking" .
