  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implicit-theories-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "laypeople's conceptions of wisdom" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implicit-theories-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/psychology-of-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implicit-theories-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The ideas about what wisdom is, who is wise and how wisdom grows that ordinary people carry around, usually without having spelled them out; psychologists study them by asking laypeople to describe, rate or nominate wise people, and contrast them with the explicit theories built by researchers." .
