<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I asking what I want from life, or what this situation is asking of me?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is there anything left for me to create, experience or stand for here, even if the outcome is out of my hands?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I watching myself so closely that it is getting in the way of what I'm trying to do?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "The project is gone, but the people I trained and what we learned stay. What do I want to build next, and how do I want to carry this?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "None of it mattered. I'll keep my head down and stop caring about the work." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A team's long-running project is cancelled after a reorganisation, and a project lead feels the past year was wasted." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Looking for meaning in contribution, relationships and chosen attitude, rather than only in outcomes you control, keeps a setback from emptying out the whole effort." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Name one thing you are creating or contributing right now, however small, and who it serves." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Name one experience or person you value that you could give more attention to this week." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "For a hardship you cannot change, decide what stance toward it you want to be able to look back on." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Turn your attention from monitoring yourself to the task or person in front of you." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Logotherapy" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/1> .
