<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is there still something I can do about this, or is it time to let the goal go and invest in another?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I learning a specific lesson from this regret, or replaying the same scene and blaming myself?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Would I speak to a friend with this regret the way I am speaking to myself?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Which choice in front of me now am I most likely to regret not making?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "I did hold back, and I wish I hadn't. What was I afraid of, and is that still true? The next lead role opens in spring, so this month I'll ask my manager for a stretch project and say plainly that I want to be considered." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "I always bottle it. I keep replaying that week and telling myself what an idiot I was, or I insist I have no regrets at all and change the subject." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "Two years ago you decided not to apply for a team-lead role; a colleague got it and is thriving, and the news of their promotion brings the old decision back." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "The wiser response accepts the regret without self-attack, extracts the lesson and turns it toward an opportunity that is still open, which is when regret is most useful." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Phenomenon> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Regret" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "learning from regret" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "life regrets" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "regrets of action and inaction" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/counterfactual-thinking> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The painful sense, on comparing what happened with what might have been, that a better outcome would have followed had you chosen differently; research finds it is the negative emotion people value most, and that it helps most when something can still be done and it is met with self-compassion rather than rumination." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/self-knowledge> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Regret" .
