<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Which way do I usually err in situations like this one, too much or too little, and am I correcting for it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I calling a choice \"balanced\" just because it sits halfway between two options, rather than because it fits the situation?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is the strength of my reaction proportionate to how serious this actually is?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "I tend to avoid conflict, so I'll lean a little firmer than feels natural: a private conversation, the specific facts, what I need by when, and a real question about what is getting in his way." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "Either I let it slide to keep the peace, or I lay it all out bluntly in front of the team so nobody can say I'm soft." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A newly promoted team lead has to tell a long-serving colleague that his reports keep arriving late and incomplete." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "The right degree of firmness depends on this person and this problem, and knowing which way you usually err tells you which way to correct, as Aristotle advised." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Principle> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Aristotle's doctrine of the mean" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Aristotelian golden mean" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "doctrine of the mean" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "mesotes" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "mesotēs" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "the mean relative to us" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/virtue-ethics> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Aristotle's teaching that each virtue of character is a settled disposition to feel and act at the intermediate point between a vice of excess and a vice of deficiency, where that point is fixed not by arithmetic but by what the situation and the person call for, as a practically wise person would judge." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/virtues-and-character> .
