<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I dismissing this objection because of its evidence, or because of who raised it and how well things have gone for me lately?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When did someone last change my mind on something important, and did I make it easy or costly for them?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Who, if anyone, can still stop me from making this decision, and have I given them what they need to do so?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I treating my organisation's success as proof of my own judgment?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "\"My recent wins are a reason to check myself, not to skip the check. Walk me through your demand figures, and let's have finance stress-test both versions before the board sees either.\" The plan is approved a quarter later at a smaller scale, with a review point." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "\"I've called it right every time so far, and the numbers will catch up with the vision. We're not slowing down for a spreadsheet.\" The analyst stops raising concerns, and the plan goes ahead unchanged." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A department head has delivered three strong years in a row and been praised in the trade press. A senior analyst warns that a proposed expansion rests on optimistic demand figures." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Recent success and praise are exactly the conditions under which leaders overpay and overreach; deliberately inviting the dissenting case and an independent check restores the feedback that power tends to cut off." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-11-13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Vice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hubris" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "CEO hubris" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "executive hubris" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "hubris syndrome" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "hubristic leadership" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "overweening pride" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "ὕβρις" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/arrogance> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An inflated, success-fed self-confidence that leads a person with power to overrate their own judgment, brush aside advice and criticism, and take overambitious risks; in ancient Greek the word named something narrower, the deliberate humiliation of others for the pleasure of feeling superior." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/wisdom-at-work> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Hubris" .
